  <h2>How to request deletion</h2>
  <p>Plate &amp; Bar is still in development, and the app and server do not yet have a delete-account feature. For now, you can ask us to delete your account and the data stored on our server by email.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Email <strong>privacy@&lt;domain TBD&gt;</strong> from the address you signed up with, with the subject "Delete my account".</li>
    <li>We confirm it is you by checking that the request comes from your sign-up email address. If needed, we reply to that address to confirm before deleting.</li>
    <li>We then delete your account. Draft target: within 30 days of the confirmed request.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>You can also ask us, by the same email, to delete specific data without deleting your account.</p>
  <!-- TODO: replace the placeholder address once a domain and mailbox are decided. -->
  <!-- TODO: when the in-app "delete everything" action (#27), the contract change (#191) and the backend DELETE /me (#192) ship, describe them here and keep the email route as a fallback. -->

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <p>Your account details, setup and health-check answers, body measurements, and the meal and workout information synced to our server.</p>
  <p>Progress photos, cycle data and lab results are never sent to our server. They stay on your phone, so the copy on your phone remains until you uninstall the app or clear its data. Once the in-app "delete everything" action is available, you will be able to wipe it from within the app.</p>

  <h2>When</h2>
  <p>Our draft target is 30 days from the confirmed request. Any data we must keep by law, and backup retention, will be stated here after legal review.</p>
